== Why the sample starts in 1957 <why-the-sample-starts-in-1957>
The dataset begins in 1913, but the estimation sample starts in 1957-01 for two documented reasons. The pre-1957 CPI-U series is a #emph[backward extrapolation]: the modern index was only linked to the earlier cost-of-living series in 1953, so the pre-1957 values are constructed rather than collected, and their dynamics reflect the construction method as much as the economy. In addition, the immediate post-war observations (1946--1948 and 1950--1951) contain one-off releases of wartime price controls, movements that are not draws from the same stochastic process as peacetime inflation.

The cost of this choice is that the project says nothing about the deflation of 1921 or 1930--1933. That is acceptable: the forecasting question concerns the inflation process that a contract written today will face, and modern US inflation has never returned to the interwar regime. @fig:history shows the full sample with the estimation window shaded, so the reader can see exactly what is excluded.

