== Stationarity: ACF, PACF and unit-root tests <sec:acf>
The autocorrelation function of $y_t$ decays with extraordinary slowness: it is $0.997$ at lag 1 and still $0.965$ at lag 12 (@tab:acfpacf and @fig:acf). The partial autocorrelation, in contrast, is essentially zero after the first lag ($- 0.005$ at lag 12). This combination is the textbook signature of a non-stationary series: the ACF of an AR(1) with $phi.alt = 0.997$ would look identical, and the PACF tells us that a single AR term would already "explain" the level, which is exactly what a unit root does.

