  caption: [
    Residual ACF and PACF with Bartlett bands. The shaded region marks lags 11--13, where the seasonal block acts; there is no spike there.
  ]
) <fig:resacf>

== Adequacy and parsimony <adequacy-and-parsimony>
@tab:neighbours compares the selected model with its immediate neighbours, all estimated on the full sample. Removing the AR term is catastrophic (AICc rises from $126.9$ to $167.8$ and the residuals fail Ljung--Box with $p < 0.001$). Removing the seasonal AR term is worse (AICc $208.8$). Adding a fourth MA term improves the AICc by only $0.4$ and the BIC not at all, so the extra parameter is not justified. The selected model is therefore the most parsimonious adequate specification in its neighbourhood, which is exactly the criterion of Chapter~6.

